<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boston</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boston is a city in the northeastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, capital of Massachusetts. Its museums hold <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-carpet">Persian carpets</a> from the classical period of Safavid weaving. The site mentions it, alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, as a home of the finest carpets produced in the royal workshops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a>, a legacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>'s artistic patronage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boston.jpg" alt="Boston" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ian Howard · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISH_WC_Boston4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
